**Definition 2.1 (Canonical preparations and two measurement subspaces).**
Let

$$
\begin{gathered}
\Delta_2=\{p=(p_0,p_+,p_-):p_i\ge0,\ \sum_ip_i=1\},\\
a(p)=\sqrt{p_0}\,d+\sqrt{p_+}\,u_++\sqrt{p_-}\,u_-,\\
V_{\rm rad}=\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb R}(d,u_+,u_-),\qquad
V_{\rm tan}=\operatorname{span}_{\mathbb R}(v_+,v_-),\\
g_* =G(\pi,\pi)\mathsf J.
\end{gathered}
\tag{2.1}
$$

The same formula for $a(p)$ is used on the nonnegative orthant when
homogeneity is useful. These subspaces are coordinates in the original
five-dimensional vector space, not tensor factors or physical ports.
Radial measurement coordinates may have any real signs.

